# The same bytes on every system: Windows checkouts keep LF line endings.
# sqlx checksums each migration file byte for byte, so a CRLF copy of one
# would make databases created from another checkout refuse to open.
* text=auto eol=lf
# Except batch files: cmd.exe misreads labels in LF-only ones (gradlew.bat).
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
# Test data stays byte for byte as it was received (the ECB's CSV uses CRLF).
crates/*/testdata/** -text
